{title: Is There No God in Israel}
{subtitle: 2 Kings 1:1–2; 1:3–6; 1:9–17; Matthew 12:24–27; 10:25; Luke 11:15–19}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Ahab is gone and Moab [Gm]rebels against the throne
A[Dm]haziah falls through the lattice in his upper room
Injured and ill he sends [Gm]word out to the coast
Go [Dm]ask Baal-Ze-bub the god of Ekron about the hope
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Is there no God in [Bb]Israel that you [Dm]must go ask
The [Gm]god of Ekron [C]for a sign [Dm]and a task
[F]You will not get up [C]from the bed [Dm]you are ly[Bb]ing on
You will surely die as [C]the Lord [Dm]has spoken
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The angel of the Lord speaks to Eli[Gm]jah the Tishbite
[Dm]Go meet the messengers of the king of Samaria
Ask them why they seek a [Gm]foreign idol's word
When the [Dm]Lord of Hosts is right here in the land
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Is there no God in Israel that [Bb]you must go ask
The [Dm]god of Ekron [Gm]for a sign and [C]a task
You will [Dm]not get up [F]from the bed you are [C]lying on
[Dm]You will surely [Bb]die as the Lord has spoken
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The first [C]captain [Dm]goes up the mountain with fifty men
Fire [Gm]comes down from heaven and con[Dm]sumes them all
The second captain falls to his knees before the prophet
Pleading for his [Gm]life and the lives of his men
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Dm]Elijah goes down with the third to the king's bedside
Saying because you sought a god [Gm]in Ekron's land
You will [Dm]not rise from the bed you lie upon
The word of the Lord is confirmed in the dust
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]Is there no God in Israel [Dm]that you must go ask
The god of Ekron for a sign and a task
You will not get up from [Bb]the bed you are ly[Dm]ing on
You will [Gm]surely die as the [C]Lord has spoken
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Dm]Every kin[F]gdom divided a[C]gainst itself [Dm]falls
Satan can[Bb]not drive out Satan
He is divid[C]ed a[Dm]gainst himself
{end_of_verse}

